From: Ahmed Amine HAOUES <ahmed-amine.haoues_ext@softathome.com>
Date: Wed, 20 May 2026 09:30:14 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 21/41] bstamld: fix missing updates of ConnectionStatus on
 auxiliary links

Problem:
- in case of bstamld, with multi-band wiphy device, backhaul scan events
(SCAN-STARTED, SCAN-FAILED) are only reported to primary link, but
auxiliary EPs are not updated, although they are part of scanned bands
- auxiliary EP's freq bands used in off-channel scanning may have scan
failure, when relative fronthaul APs are active, but they are not
handled as no events is reported by wpa_supp

Fix:
- Distribute the "SCAN-STARTED" and "SCAN-FAILED" events to received on
primary bstamld link, to running auxiliary links and not having their
own wpactrl connexions.
- mark secondary bstamld links as passive while main link is connecting
- handle DISCONNECTED event regardless profile availability, in order
to ensure main link status update

References: PPM-4222
Signed-off-by: Ahmed Amine HAOUES <ahmed-amine.haoues_ext@softathome.com>
Upstream-Status: Backport [https://gitlab.com/prpl-foundation/prplmesh/pwhm/plugins/pwhm/-/commit/f4ff49eb05f48cadebe5f1596d54f97828d084d1]
---
 src/Plugin/wifiGen_eventHandlers.c |  10 +--
 src/Plugin/wifiGen_fsm.c           | 101 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 2 files changed, 96 insertions(+), 15 deletions(-)

